    "created_at": "2026-01-09T09:06:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-09T09:06:08Z",
    "body": "At WHATNOT, we agreed that limited commands should be per element type. So, if a command can run on, say, a `div`, then command events will always fire for that command on `div`s.\r\n\r\nA number of future commands, such as scrolling, will be able to happen on multiple elements. I guess it'll be interesting to see what we do there in terms of replaced elements (like `img`), but that's for another day.\r\n\r\nI'll update the PR.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
